message.content:
Looking at the failure: peer-b26 expects `phase=1` but the implementation produces `phase=2`. Tracing the sequence, the bug is in the phase transition logic. The current code uses OR (`prev_phase = 2 OR pv >= setpoint`) when it should use AND (`prev_phase = 2 AND pv >= setpoint`). 

Also, `prev_startBtn` is not updated before the early RETURN in both the abort and start edge branches — this would cause spurious rising edges on the next scan after abort/start.

```json
{"edits":[
  {"old": "    abortBtn THEN
    phase := 9;
    prev_startBtn := startBtn;
    RETURN;
END_IF;

IF startRising THEN
    phase   := 1;
    elapsed := 0;
    timeout := FALSE;
    prev_startBtn := startBtn;
    RETURN;
END_IF;", "new": "    abortBtn THEN
    phase := 9;
    prev_startBtn := startBtn;
    RETURN;
END_IF;

IF startRising THEN
    phase   := 1;
    elapsed := 0;
    timeout := FALSE;
    prev_startBtn := startBtn;
    RETURN;
END_IF;"},
  {"old": "        IF pv >= setpoint THEN
            phase := 2;
        ELSE
            phase := 1;
        END_IF;", "new": "        IF (prev_phase = 2) AND (pv >= setpoint) THEN
            phase := 2;
        ELSE
            phase := 1;
        END_IF;"}
]}
```
